The baseline must be constructed first (e.g. with \code{\link[=import_baseline]{import_baseline()}}).
\code{T_loss} is the number of forecast quarters over which the loss is
counted; \code{T_instrument} is the number of quarters of policy shocks chosen
(i.e. over which policy is optimised). Both must lie between 1 and the
number of quarters from \code{forecast_start} to \code{forecast_end}. Under
discretion, \code{T_loss} must also be at least \code{T_instrument}: policy is re-set
in each instrument quarter to minimise the loss from then on, so every
instrument quarter must fall within the loss horizon.

\code{commit} selects the strategy: \code{"disc"} for discretion, or one of two
forms of commitment - \code{"commit"}, in which commitment starts today, and
\code{"timeless"}, in which commitment is assumed to have been in place since
some past date, \code{preloss_start} (see below). Loss variables are
penalised as deviations from zero; to target a non-zero value, construct
a gap variable by subtracting the target from the actual variable, add it
to the baseline (and vintages), e.g. \code{Inflation_gap_loss}, and use it as
the loss variable.

For a model whose policy shocks are all unanticipated - because
\code{use_cd = FALSE}, \code{lambda = 0}, or the model has no anticipated shocks
(\verb{<shock>_1}, \verb{<shock>_2}, ...) - commitment and discretion coincide. An
error is raised if the model's impulse responses or anticipated shocks
do not cover the required horizon (including any commitment history).

See \code{\link[=get_policy_scenarios]{get_policy_scenarios()}} to run a list of strategies across a list of
models at once (as the dashboard does).

\code{baseline} has a quarterly \code{date} column and includes the output, loss,
constraint, and instrument variables named in \code{policy_strategy}, each
column keyed by either \code{model}'s own dynare code or (as in a canonical
baseline returned by \code{\link[=import_baseline]{import_baseline()}}) its display name. The returned
paths are rescaled and labelled with model metadata.
