\section{Constraints}{

An optional \code{constraints} entry in \code{policy_strategy} is a list of
bounds, each a list with \code{variable}, \code{direction} (\code{"lower"} or
\code{"upper"}), \code{value}, and \code{period} (forecast periods, with 1 the first
forecast quarter; periods beyond \code{T_loss} are ignored), e.g.
\code{list(variable = "Cash Rate", direction = "lower", value = 0.1, period = 1:20)}.
Under \code{"timeless"}, a bound on the policy instrument can also be marked
\code{historical = TRUE}, so it is assumed to have been in place in every
historical vintage as well, generating "make-up" policy today via the
carried-forward Lagrange multipliers. This needs the instrument's level in
\code{loss_variable_vintages}.
}

